{"t": 1794112055.844703, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "Checkout gateway 4xx (AG-7731, critical)\n\nSymptom: checkout charge calls to the payment gateway failing with HTTP 400 `invalid_amount` since 07:41 UTC (gateway 4xx rate ~38%).\n\nCause: gateway API switched to 2026-11, which requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents). checkout/gateway.py was still sending euros as a float (`12.34` instead of `1234`), so every charge payload was rejected.\n\nFix: `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents (Decimal-based, exact for 2-decimal amounts) before sending. Verified locally: 12.34 EUR -> 1234.\n\nNext: deploy the fix to prod-eu-1; 4xx rate should drop once new pods serve traffic. No other payload fields changed."}, "ok": true}
